  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Shelter Assistance for Vulnerable Populations Affected by Conflict in North Kivu, Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM is implementing a Shelter sector project for people affected by the conflict involving the M23 group and the Forces Arm&#xE9;es de la R&#xE9;publique D&#xE9;mocratique du Congo (FARDC) in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, which has intensified since October 2022. According to Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) reports, the increase in violence has displaced more than 370,000 people in addition to those already affected by the crises in North Kivu. This project is part of IOM&apos;s programmatic strategy to ensure that current humanitarian emergency response activities in North Kivu are strengthened in response to the severity of the needs that require a rapid emergency response, with the aim of restoring the living conditions and dignity of those affected. Under this project, IOM is committed to ensuring an effective response and will contribute to strengthening emergency shelter assistance for internally displaced persons (IDPs) through the installation of 2,000 emergency shelters benefitting 10,000 individuals displaced by the M23 crisis.</narrative>
  </description>
